+// Kinoko patch (kinoko: patches/burrito-musl-runtime.patch).
+//
+// The precompiled ERTS names MUSL_RUNTIME_PATH (/tmp/libc-musl-<sha>.so) as
+// its ELF interpreter, so the path cannot move. Upstream reuses any file
+// already there, so on a shared host another user could plant it and run
+// code as whoever starts the binary next. Here the file is used only when it
+// is trusted: a regular file owned by this user (or root), not writable by
+// group or others, executable, byte-for-byte the embedded runtime, in a directory that is
+// sticky or private (so nobody else can swap it afterwards). A missing file,
+// or a stale one of ours, is written to a private temp file and renamed into
+// place. Anything else stops the start with a message; it is never loaded.
+const MuslState = enum { trusted, missing, ours_stale, foreign };
+
